  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Interferon alfa-2b is an immunostimulant medicine used for cancers such as melanoma, hairy cell leukemia, follicular lymphoma and multiple myeloma, and for chronic hepatitis B and C infections. It is an approved drug, though some European Union products have been withdrawn.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4391540&quot;>Wikidata Q4391540</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>interferon alfa-2b</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L03AB05</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00105&quot;>DB00105</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4391540&quot;>Q4391540</a></td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>746.5 g/mol (Drugs.Common (25.09))</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
